:PNLGRP.
:COPYR.(C) Copyright Quartz Systems 2026.
:HELP NAME=ADDLICKEY.Add License Key Information (ADDLICKEY)
:P.Use the Add License Key Information (ADDLICKEY) command to add a
license key; a Quartz key is 18 groups of 6.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDLICKEY/LICKEYINP'.License key input (LICKEYINP)
:P.The license key input for this command.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *PROMPT, *LICKEYFILE.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDLICKEY/PRDID'.Product identifier (PRDID)
:P.A product identifier&colon. seven characters, QS00SS1 for example.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 7 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDLICKEY/LICTRM'.License term (LICTRM)
:P.The license term of the product, for example V7 or V7R1.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 6 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDLICKEY/FEATURE'.Feature (FEATURE)
:P.The feature code of the product.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 4 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDLICKEY/SERIAL'.System serial number (SERIAL)
:P.The system serial number for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LOCAL:EPK.
:PD.This system.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 8 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDLICKEY/PRCGRP'.Processor group (PRCGRP)
:P.The processor group for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ANY:EPK.
:PD.Any value matches.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 4 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDLICKEY/LICKEY'.License key (LICKEY)
:P.The license key for this command.
:P.Up to 18 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 6 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDLICKEY/USGLMT'.Usage limit (USGLMT)
:P.The usage limit for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NOMAX:EPK.
:PD.No limit.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 7 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDLICKEY/EXPDATE'.Expiration date (EXPDATE)
:P.The date after which the object or file can be deleted or
overwritten. *PERM means it never expires.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.It never expires.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDLICKEY/VNDDTA'.Vendor data (VNDDTA)
:P.The vendor data for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 8 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDLICKEY/LICKEYFILE'.License key stream file (LICKEYFILE)
:P.The license key stream file for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 256 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CHGLICINF.Change License Information (CHGLICINF)
:P.Use the Change License Information (CHGLICINF) command to change a
product's license information.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGLICINF/PRDID'.Product identifier (PRDID)
:P.A product identifier&colon. seven characters, QS00SS1 for example.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 7 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGLICINF/LICTRM'.License term (LICTRM)
:P.The license term of the product, for example V7 or V7R1.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 6 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGLICINF/FEATURE'.Feature (FEATURE)
:P.The feature code of the product.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 4 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGLICINF/USGLMT'.Usage limit (USGLMT)
:P.The usage limit for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NOMAX:EPK.
:PD.No limit.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 7 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGLICINF/THRESHOLD'.Threshold (THRESHOLD)
:P.The threshold for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*CALC:EPK.
:PD.The system calculates the value.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 7 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *USGLMT.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGLICINF/MSGQ'.Message queue (MSGQ)
:P.The message queue that receives the messages the command or the
object sends.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGLICINF/LOG'.Log (LOG)
:P.The log for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=DSPLICKEY.Display License Key Information (DSPLICKEY)
:P.Use the Display License Key Information (DSPLICKEY) command to show
the license keys added to the system.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPLICKEY/PRDID'.Product identifier (PRDID)
:P.A product identifier&colon. seven characters, QS00SS1 for example.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 7 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPLICKEY/LICTRM'.License term (LICTRM)
:P.The license term of the product, for example V7 or V7R1.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 6 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPLICKEY/FEATURE'.Feature (FEATURE)
:P.The feature code of the product.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 4 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPLICKEY/SERIAL'.System serial number (SERIAL)
:P.The system serial number for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LOCAL:EPK.
:PD.This system.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 8 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPLICKEY/OUTPUT'.Output (OUTPUT)
:P.Where the command sends what it produces&colon. to the display of an
interactive job, or to a spooled file of the job's printer file. Some
commands can also write it to a database file.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*:EPK.
:PD.The output is shown at the display of an interactive job, and
printed for a batch job.
:PT.:PK.*PRINT:EPK.
:PD.The output is printed with the job's spooled output.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *LICKEYFILE.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPLICKEY/LICKEYFILE'.License key stream file (LICKEYFILE)
:P.The license key stream file for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 256 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=RMVLICKEY.Remove License Key Information (RMVLICKEY)
:P.Use the Remove License Key Information (RMVLICKEY) command to remove
license keys.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVLICKEY/PRDID'.Product identifier (PRDID)
:P.A product identifier&colon. seven characters, QS00SS1 for example.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 7 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVLICKEY/LICTRM'.License term (LICTRM)
:P.The license term of the product, for example V7 or V7R1.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 6 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVLICKEY/FEATURE'.Feature (FEATURE)
:P.The feature code of the product.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 4 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVLICKEY/SERIAL'.System serial number (SERIAL)
:P.The system serial number for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LOCAL:EPK.
:PD.This system.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 8 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVLICKEY/PRCGRP'.Processor group (PRCGRP)
:P.The processor group for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*ANY:EPK.
:PD.Any value matches.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 4 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=WRKLICINF.Work with License Information (WRKLICINF)
:P.Use the Work with License Information (WRKLICINF) command to work
with the license information of products.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKLICINF/PRDID'.Product identifier (PRDID)
:P.A product identifier&colon. seven characters, QS00SS1 for example.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *INSTALLED.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKLICINF/OUTPUT'.Output (OUTPUT)
:P.Where the command sends what it produces&colon. to the display of an
interactive job, or to a spooled file of the job's printer file. Some
commands can also write it to a database file.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*:EPK.
:PD.The output is shown at the display of an interactive job, and
printed for a batch job.
:PT.:PK.*PRINT:EPK.
:PD.The output is printed with the job's spooled output.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
